= Study parameters and comparison table

This note records the parameters used when two coders compared annotations across codebook editions. The table below is read together with the prose rules that precede it.

Each parameter is recorded once per frozen snapshot and never edited in place after the freeze. A later change to a parameter value creates a new snapshot rather than a correction.

Passages that disagree between coders are retained in the record with both coder identifiers attached. Disagreements are counted per passage, and the count is reported beside each parameter value.

The comparison table lists the parameters that were frozen with the pilot study. Supporting and challenging links are stored separately and are not summarised by the table.

Analytical values are computed only from the frozen survey rows, and presentation formats never influence them. When evidence conflicts, both links are kept and the conflict is reported as it stands.

| Parameter | Frozen value | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Participants | 30 interviews | Four withdrawals recorded |
| Codebook edition | Second edition | One broad code replaced by two codes |
| Disagreements | 17 passages | Retained with both coder identifiers |
| Snapshot | 2026-09-08 freeze | Manifest lists its own members |
| Presentation | Recorded separately | Never changes an analytical value |

After the table, the review session closes with a short written summary that names the snapshot used and every conflict that remains visible in the trace.
